    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Humidity is analyzed as Absolute, Relative, and Specific humidity, each responding differently to temperature changes.",
        "Clouds are systematically classified by altitude into High, Middle, Low, and Vertical development categories.",
        "Precipitation occurs through three main mechanisms: Convectional, Orographic, and Cyclonic rainfall.",
        "Condensation is the core atmospheric process that transforms water vapor into cloud droplets and rainfall."
